  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The application has failed to demonstrate that the existing HMO (sui generis) does not meet appropriate standards and if this is the case, has no realistic prospect of doing so. In the absence of adequate replacement HMO provision, the proposal would result in the unjustified net loss of HMO floorspace and harm to housing provision within the borough. For the given reasons the proposal is contrary to Policy LP29B of the Wandsworth Local Plan and Policy H9 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed development, by reason of layout and design would fail to provide an acceptable standard of accommodation for future occupiers as the proposed bedrooms within the ground floor Flat 1 fall short of the requirement to provide at least one double space; and a section drawing has not been provided to demonstrate the satisfactory floor to ceiling heights to the ground floor flat. The proposal is therefore contrary to policy LP27 of the Wandsworth Local Plan (2023), policy D6 of the London Plan (2021) and the Technical Housing Standards - Nationally Described Space Standard (2015).",
    "Reason : 3 - In dealing with this application the Council has implemented the requirement in the National Planning Policy Framework to make available detailed advice in the form of our statutory policies in the Local Plan as well as offering a full pre application advice service. However, we have been unable to seek solutions to problems as the proposal is clearly contrary to our statutory policies and negotiation could not overcome the reasons for refusal."
  ],
